TUnit uses `[Before(…)]` and `[After(…)]` attributes with a `HookType` enum to control scope. Here's a sketch for each:

## 1. Before/After Every Test (method-level)

```csharp
public class MyTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public void ResetDatabase()
    {
        // Runs before each [Test] in this class
        InMemoryDb.Reset();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public void Cleanup()
    {
        // Runs after each [Test] in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public void OrderIsCreated() { /* ... */ }
}
```

## 2. Once Per Class (class-level)

```csharp
public class MyTests
{
    private static HttpClient _client;

    [Before(Class)]
    public static void OpenFixture()
    {
        // Runs once before the first test in this class
        _client = new HttpClient();
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static void DisposeFixture()
    {
        // Runs once after the last test in this class
        _client.Dispose();
    }

    [Test]
    public void GetReturnsOk() { /* ... */ }
}
```

> Class-level hooks **must be `static`**.

## 3. Once Per Assembly (assembly-level)

```csharp
// Can live in any class in the assembly — often a dedicated "hooks" file
public class GlobalHooks
{
    private static WireMockServer _server;

    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static void StartWireMock()
    {
        _server = WireMockServer.Start();
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static void StopWireMock()
    {
        _server.Stop();
    }
}
```

## 4. Once Per Entire Test Session (test-run-level)

```csharp
public class SessionHooks
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static void ApplyMigrations()
    {
        // Runs once at the very start of the test process
        Database.Migrate();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static void TearDown()
    {
        // Runs once at the very end
        Database.Drop();
    }
}
```

## Summary Table

| Scope | Attribute | Must be static? |
|-------|-----------|-----------------|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | No |
| Class | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | Yes |
| Assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | Yes |
| Session | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | Yes |

The `HookType` values (`Test`, `Class`, `Assembly`, `TestSession`) are imported via `using static TUnit.Core.HookType;` (or fully qualified). Async variants (`Task`/`ValueTask` return types) are supported — just change the return type.
